+## 3. Decisions and rationale
+1. **The lead's build, not my own.** The lead's note says to serve `<scratch>/cycle-beta6-dist` and not rebuild it
+   (this replaces the template's build step). Its `app.js`, `viz/chart.js`, `viz/map.js`, `api.js` and
+   `features/insights.js` are byte-identical to d98a9f0's `public/` (only the generated `config.js` differs), so
+   the build is the branch head. Served by `scripts/cycle/serve.mjs` with a pid file. No server-mode check was
+   needed beyond the suite's own server tests (`[D-20]` starts a `MELON_CHANNEL=beta` server).
+2. **Card text for every posting, outside the browser.** The list is windowed, so reading 13,980 Amazon cards in
+   the page is slow. `cards.mjs` lifts `payPill` and the helpers it reaches out of `public/app.js` by name (the
+   method of `test/salary-audit.test.js`, resolving missing names until it runs) and runs it on every paid posting
+   of the build's lists. Each candidate it found was then confirmed in the real UI (card and drawer).
+3. **Tests read the build's data, not hard-coded IDs.** Each `[D-n]` test finds its case in the build's own data
+   (`getJobs`) and asserts on the screen, so it keeps testing the defect on a new crawl and passes when the defect
+   is gone: `[D-38]` any Google "Fellow, …" title; `[D-39]` any Amazon posting whose rows share a place name;
+   `[D-40]` any term or part-time posting with different pay per place; `[D-41]` any St./St/Saint label pair with
+   no state; `[D-42]` any "X, US" label beside an "X" label; `[D-43]` any chart range end in the millions not
+   written as the card writes it; `[D-44]` any 1–2-role Location row above a 100-role row.
+4. **Severity.** High: wrong output on a core task for most users. Medium: wrong output a user acts on, in a
+   supported state (D-38 hides Google's highest-paid posting behind a wrong estimate; D-39 hides which state each
+   remote pay range is for). Low: labelling, consistency and ordering.
+5. **Known items are evidence, not new bugs.** The brief's known list (MR-23, MR-26, MR-28, MR-29, MR-33 to
+   MR-35, MR-37 to MR-42, the Amazon Insights task) and the lead's own round-3 follow-ups (NVIDIA OTE and Google
+   degree-line "· N levels", Amazon monthly minimums without "from", Town and Country, SA-1's Juice on a level
+   span) were seen on the desktop and are listed under Notes with counts.
+6. **The Amazon preview was tested by holding the list.** A route (scripts) or the test's own server (e2e) delays
+   `api/jobs/amazon.json` by 6–9 s, so the preview can be read, clicked and compared with the list that replaces it.
+7. **Load.** Other agents ran throughout: load average 4 to 23 (noted at each timing). Timings are upper bounds.
+8. **Full e2e with the lead's build as `dist`.** Several suites read only `ROOT/dist`. The worktree's `dist` is a
+   symlink to the lead's build (not the shared checkout's `dist/`, which I never touch), and `BETA_QA_DIST` points
+   at it too. The suite's screenshot rewrites land in this worktree's `docs/screenshots/` and are restored after.
